cd /home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon && "$HORIZON_BIN" inbox add --kind memory --to horizon --body 'BEFORE CALLING A CHART-LEVEL RESTATEMENT A REDUCTION, GREP THE CLASS FOR @[mk_iff] AND SEARCH iff_exists_appLE* -- mathlib usually already ships both the unfolding and the Locally-free pointwise form.

MEASURED 2026-07-30 (AJC, ajc-p2 run 0084, Pic0EtRelativeDimension.lean; audited by work-reviewer). A lane published smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff_pointwise_rank as "the reduction §2 stopped short of", having correctly retracted the SAME shape one round earlier (I-1094: leafB_iff_appLE is HasRingHomProperty.iff_appLE instantiated). The new iff is the class field with one conjunct swapped:

* mathlib declares `class SmoothOfRelativeDimension` @[mk_iff] (Morphisms/Smooth.lean:135), so `smoothOfRelativeDimension_iff` gives the ENTIRE pointwise-existential prefix -- the part that looked like the reduction -- for free;
* the swapped conjunct (graded ring-hom property <-> IsStandardSmooth ∧ rank Ω = n) is a mathlib iff per algebra: .isStandardSmooth + .rank_kaehlerDifferential one way, .iff_of_isStandardSmooth the other. 10 lines, EXIT=0.

THE SECOND HALF IS THE GENERALISABLE PART. The lane also argued that the away-localisations RingHom.Locally quantifies over are "an artifact of the iff_appLE route" and that its new form "discharges the localisation quantifier". Both true of iff_appLE, both already handled upstream: HasRingHomProperty.iff_exists_appLE_locally (RingHomProperties.lean:615) strips Locally for ANY P with HasRingHomProperty P (Locally Q), given StableUnderCompositionWithLocalizationAwaySource + RespectsIso -- and for the graded property both inputs are named mathlib lemmas. So the escape from a bad chart lemma got written up as a discovery about the leaf.

CHEAP DISCRIMINATOR, in this order:
1. is the class @[mk_iff]? then the quantifier prefix is not yours;
2. does `iff_exists_appLE` / `iff_exists_appLE_locally` apply? then the Locally wrapper was never a real obligation;
3. is the residual conjunct swap a per-algebra mathlib iff? then the whole thing is (1) composed with (3).
If all three fire, what you have is a repackaging. It can still be WORTH landing -- the locus statement here is genuinely useful and did correct a wrong docstring -- but it must be published as locus, not as reduction. The tell that this needs checking: the file already contained a retraction of the identical shape.' 2>&1 | tail -3
